    "details": {
      "alignment": "Unaligned (charmed)",
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "Toad, helm-bound"
      },
      "cr": 2,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Fawful's Forces packet sheet — Vat-Warped Thrall.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-forge-packets.py</code> from the NPC Forge roster <code>data/forge/fawfuls-forces.json</code> (entry <code>vat-warped-thrall</code>): Small humanoid (Toad, helm-bound), Unaligned (charmed); CR 2 (proficiency +2, to hit +4 with STR); AC 12 (vine-knit skin), hit points 39 (6d6+18), speed 25 ft.. A GM scene kit for the Fawful's Forces article's present (1040 BF), not a filed event; the faction article stays the authority.</p><p>The occupation's worst habit. A Toad taken in the castle or the town, fitted with a Hypno-Helm, left in the vats until the vines took and the helm no longer needed to talk. The faction article says Fawful's forces \"mechanize, mutate\"; the thrall is the second word done to a person. The garrison uses them as porters, as sappers and, when a fight starts, as the thing between the party and the Beanish officer.</p><p>This is the moral encounter in the packet, and the sheet says so. A thrall can be freed in the middle of a fight by anyone willing to spend an action and a good roll on the helm instead of the wrench; a thrall can also be killed, and that is a citizen of Toad Town dead, which the Peach Loyalists and the Toads will hear about. Fire stops the vine healing; nothing else does.</p><p><strong>Role:</strong> helm-bound captive · <strong>tier:</strong> vat-work · <strong>folder:</strong> Fawful's Furious Freaks / The Bean Garrison.</p><h3>Art</h3><p>Token plate <code>portraits/fawfuls-forces/vat-warped-thrall.png</code> — NPC Forge render, seed 410010, cut from a flat #FF00FF field. Prompt: <q>Clean cel-shaded cartoon character art in the style of Mario & Luigi RPG concept art, bold dark outlines, flat colours, simple shading. A small Toad person with a red and white spotted mushroom cap, a green Hypno-Helm visor with a glowing hypnotic spiral fused over the eyes, a blank slack expression, a blue vest and white trousers, thorny green vines growing over the arms and legs, holding a brass wrench. Full body, whole figure visible, three-quarter view, centred, isolated on a plain flat solid magenta background (#FF00FF), no floor, no ground shadow, no text, no border.</q></p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
